  "id": "ambiguous-figure",
  "term": "ambiguous figure",
  "definition": "An ambiguous figure is a visual stimulus that stays physically the same while perception switches back and forth between different, mutually exclusive interpretations. It is used to study internally driven changes in perception because the reversals come from endogenous brain processes rather than from changes in the stimulus.",
