      "reasons": [
        "The definition claims that ambiguous figures are “used to study internally driven changes in perception” and that the reversals come “from endogenous brain processes rather than from changes in the stimulus.” The packet supports that, during observation, the stimulus remains unchanged and perception alternates via “endogenous reversals,” but it does not explicitly state that ambiguous figures are used (in general) to study “internally driven changes in perception,” only that the authors use them in their specific study to understand altered endogenous brain dynamics."
